{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "cluster_density_aware",
  "intent": "Introduce a direct cluster_density term rewarding candidates embedded in dense unvisited neighborhoods, targeting the cluster family where interior nodes enable efficient intra-cluster traversal. Keep parent's return-distance with progress modulation (helps uniform) and nonlinear regret correction (helps all). Slightly relax the spread penalty because high-density cluster cores naturally exhibit low spread, making the parent penalty redundant or slightly harmful there. The new term is near-zero on uniform instances (density is uniformly low), neutral on grid (moderate density variation), and strongly positive on clusters, shifting selection toward dense-region interiors.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "return_aware"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    r = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    s = f['spread']\n    denom = 0.5 + nr\n    if denom < 1e-9:\n        denom = 1e-9\n    return -d + 0.2 * cd + 0.25 * (1 + p) * rd + 0.1 * r + 0.1 * r / denom - 0.03 * s",
  "source": "live_llm",
